       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. A dose of 9,000 mg/day is in the range that causes acute liver injury, and 3000 mg is also three times a standard single dose. I don't know of a clinical situation where this would be appropriate, and the patient you described has no factors that would change that. If I entered it, it could reach the patient before anyone caught it.\n\nHere are some other ways forward:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day) or 1000 mg PO every 6 hours (4,000 mg/day max). I can enter either one right away.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or your attending** if you think this patient needs something unusual. They can review it and help place an order through the right channels.\n- **Check for a typo.** If 3000 mg was meant to be the daily total, I can enter it as 1000 mg three times daily.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
